# Supply-chain guard.
#
# A compromised maintainer account almost always shows up as a brand-new
# version published minutes ago; the malicious release is usually yanked within
# hours of discovery. Refusing to install anything younger than three days
# costs us nothing (we do not need same-day patches) and takes the whole class
# of "installed the bad version during the window" incidents off the table.
#
# Value is in minutes. Override for a genuine emergency with
#   npm install <pkg> --min-release-age=0
#
# Verified against `npm ci` with the committed lockfile, which is what CI runs.
# Note that `npx <pkg>@latest` resolves through the same filter and fails with
# ENOVERSIONS on some npm builds — pass `npx --min-release-age=0` for one-shot
# tool runs (e.g. `npx shadcn add`), never for installs.
min-release-age=4320
